PREDICTION: q(M) is locked to powers of 2 exactly when the amendment
cycle length L is a power of 2 (then F2[y]/(y^L-1) is local, 1+y is
nilpotent).  An odd factor L' > 1 contributes F_{2^d} with d=ord_{L'}(2),
where 1+zeta is a unit of ODD order dividing 2^d-1.
  L=2 -> only 2-powers.  L=3 -> F4, 1+w = w^2 has order 3.
  L=4 -> only 2-powers.  L=5 -> F16, orders dividing 15.
  L=6 -> odd part 3 -> order 3.

